WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.841 --> 00:00:16.003
The town clock was striking 8 p.m.

2
00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:19.364
when I arrived in Millcote on that raw October evening.

3
00:00:20.385 --> 00:00:24.787
No one from Thornfield was there to meet me, so I went into the inn to wait.

4
00:00:25.828 --> 00:00:29.430
After half an hour, I finally thought to ask a waiter for help.

5
00:00:33.588 --> 00:00:34.248
"Is your name Eyre, miss?"

6
00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:34.529
he asked.

7
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:35.969
"If so, a person has just arrived for you."

8
00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.532
I jumped up, took my muff and umbrella, and hurried outside.

9
00:00:41.613 --> 00:00:44.014
A man was standing by a one-horse carriage.

10
00:00:45.095 --> 00:00:47.437
I stepped in and he hoisted my trunk aboard.

11
00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:53.700
Two hours passed before we drove through a pair of gates and arrived outside a large house.

12
00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:59.064
Candlelight gleamed from only one window; the rest of the house was dark.

13
00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:04.253
A maid opened the carriage door and asked me to follow her into the house.

14
00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:11.095
She led me to a snug room, where a little old woman sat knitting by the fire while

15
00:01:11.175 --> 00:01:12.576
a cat slept on the rug.

16
00:01:13.696 --> 00:01:16.077
I couldn't imagine a more reassuring scene.

17
00:01:16.097 --> 00:01:18.797
"Mrs. Fairfax?"

18
00:01:19.257 --> 00:01:19.698
I said.

19
00:01:19.718 --> 00:01:21.738
"Yes, my dear.

20
00:01:22.778 --> 00:01:24.199
Come sit by the fire.

21
00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:28.000
You must be cold after your tedious journey.

22
00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.269
John drives so slowly."

23
00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:32.969
Then Mrs.

24
00:01:33.029 --> 00:01:37.831
Fairfax said to the maid, "Leah, bring us some hot tea and sandwiches."

25
00:01:39.051 --> 00:01:40.231
Meanwhile Mrs.

26
00:01:40.271 --> 00:01:44.173
Fairfax went away to make sure that my luggage was carried to my room.

27
00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:50.034
When she returned, she cleared the table of her knitting to make space for the tea tray.

28
00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:55.676
I was confused by all the attention that my new employer was lavishing on me.

29
00:01:56.736 --> 00:01:59.557
"Will I have the pleasure of seeing Miss Fairfax tonight?"

30
00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:00.517
I asked.

31
00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:03.238
"Oh, you mean Miss Varens!

32
00:02:04.398 --> 00:02:06.119
Adele Varens is your pupil."

33
00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:08.440
"Then she isn't your daughter?"

34
00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.640
"No, I have no family."

35
00:02:12.581 --> 00:02:17.102
I found this perplexing but didn't want to be impolite by asking more questions.

36
00:02:17.122 --> 00:02:22.104
"It will be quite pleasant now that you're here," Mrs.

37
00:02:22.144 --> 00:02:23.104
Fairfax went on.

38
00:02:24.328 --> 00:02:29.131
"Leah and John are decent people and so is John's wife, Mary, who is the cook.

39
00:02:30.291 --> 00:02:36.835
But they're only servants, and one must keep them at a distance for fear of losing one's authority.

40
00:02:38.216 --> 00:02:40.717
Oh, here I am going on, and you're tired."

41
00:02:42.038 --> 00:02:46.860
As she showed me upstairs, I felt that the whole house was cold and cheerless.

42
00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:51.163
I was glad to find that my own room was warm and welcoming.

43
00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:55.357
After a long day, I had reached a safe haven.

44
00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:59.980
The next morning I dressed with care in my plain black frock.

45
00:03:01.141 --> 00:03:06.345
Looking in the mirror, I wished that I were taller and prettier, but I didn't know why I

46
00:03:06.405 --> 00:03:07.365
had these feelings.

47
00:03:08.566 --> 00:03:12.789
I went down the imposing oak staircase to the hall and out the front door.

48
00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:17.112
Crossing the lawn, I turned and looked back at the house.

49
00:03:18.993 --> 00:03:24.001
It was three stories high, large but not imposing—a gentleman's estate.

50
00:03:25.101 --> 00:03:27.842
Mrs. Fairfax appeared at the door and called to me.

51
00:03:27.862 --> 00:03:30.643
"How do you like Thornfield?"

52
00:03:31.023 --> 00:03:31.604
she asked.

53
00:03:32.704 --> 00:03:33.604
I walked up to her.

54
00:03:33.624 --> 00:03:36.145
"I like it very much."

55
00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:39.727
"It is a pretty place," she agreed.

56
00:03:39.747 --> 00:03:43.548
"But I fear it will start to decline unless Mr.

57
00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:48.831
Rochester decides to reside here permanently or at least to visit more often."

58
00:03:48.851 --> 00:03:51.111
"Mr. Rochester!"

59
00:03:51.512 --> 00:03:52.232
I exclaimed.

60
00:03:53.312 --> 00:03:53.893
"Who's that?"

61
00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:59.577
"The owner of Thornfield," she said, as if everyone knew that fact.

62
00:03:59.597 --> 00:04:02.820
"But I thought Thornfield belonged to you."

63
00:04:03.941 --> 00:04:05.562
Now I was truly confused.

64
00:04:05.583 --> 00:04:07.444
"To me?

65
00:04:08.645 --> 00:04:10.447
Bless you, child, what an idea!"

66
00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:12.248
Mrs. Fairfax smiled.

67
00:04:12.268 --> 00:04:17.733
"I'm only the housekeeper, though I am a distant relative of Mr.

68
00:04:17.813 --> 00:04:21.256
Rochester. His mother was a Fairfax."

69
00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.020
"And my pupil?"

70
00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.781
"She's Mr.

71
00:04:25.841 --> 00:04:27.301
Rochester's ward.

72
00:04:28.461 --> 00:04:30.502
He asked me to find a governess for her.

73
00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:33.803
Here she comes now with her nurse, Sophie."

74
00:04:34.903 --> 00:04:37.924
A small child of perhaps seven or eight ran up to us.

75
00:04:39.084 --> 00:04:41.505
Her long, golden curls reached her waist.

76
00:04:41.525 --> 00:04:43.766
"Is this my governess?"

77
00:04:44.206 --> 00:04:48.487
she asked her nurse in French, and the woman responded in the same language.

78
00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:50.627
"Are they from France?"

79
00:04:51.088 --> 00:04:51.788
I asked Mrs.

80
00:04:51.828 --> 00:04:53.944
Fairfax. "Yes.

81
00:04:54.624 --> 00:04:57.105
I was glad when you advertised that you speak French.

82
00:04:58.305 --> 00:05:00.146
I can't speak a word of it myself."

83
00:05:01.286 --> 00:05:05.727
We went into breakfast, where I conversed with Adele and soon learned that Mr.

84
00:05:05.807 --> 00:05:09.048
Rochester had brought her to England after her mother died.

85
00:05:10.929 --> 00:05:15.850
After breakfast Adele and I went to the library, which had been set up as our schoolroom.

86
00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:22.052
She was not used to school, so I taught her only a little that morning although I talked

87
00:05:22.092 --> 00:05:23.072
to her a great deal.

88
00:05:24.336 --> 00:05:26.977
At noontime I allowed her to return to her nurse.

89
00:05:28.198 --> 00:05:32.399
I decided to occupy myself until lunch by drawing some sketches for her.

90
00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.861
As I was going to fetch my paper and pencils, I saw Mrs.

91
00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:42.203
Fairfax in the dining room—a stately room with purple chairs and walnut-paneled walls.

92
00:05:43.404 --> 00:05:46.785
"What a beautiful room, and you keep it so nicely!"

93
00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:47.886
I exclaimed.

94
00:05:47.906 --> 00:05:53.448
"Except for the fact that the air feels chilly, one would think the room was used daily."

95
00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.701
"I like to have everything ready for Mr.

96
00:05:56.761 --> 00:06:00.603
Rochester, although he rarely visits," she explained.

97
00:06:00.623 --> 00:06:06.366
"But when he does, it's always at the last minute, and he doesn't like the bustle of cleaning

98
00:06:06.446 --> 00:06:07.507
going on around him."

99
00:06:07.527 --> 00:06:10.408
"Is he a fussy man?"

100
00:06:10.428 --> 00:06:12.969
"Not particularly so."

101
00:06:12.989 --> 00:06:15.731
"Do people generally like him?"

102
00:06:15.751 --> 00:06:17.612
"Oh yes.

103
00:06:18.784 --> 00:06:24.407
The family has always been respected here, though he is a bit peculiar."

104
00:06:24.427 --> 00:06:27.928
"Peculiar? In what way?"

105
00:06:27.948 --> 00:06:29.989
"I don't know.

106
00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.071
You feel it when you speak to him.

107
00:06:34.111 --> 00:06:36.552
You can't always tell whether he's serious or not."

108
00:06:37.753 --> 00:06:41.895
This made me feel curious about our employer's character, but Mrs.

109
00:06:41.955 --> 00:06:43.756
Fairfax said nothing more about it.

110
00:06:44.956 --> 00:06:48.838
When we left the dining room, she volunteered to show me the whole house.

111
00:06:50.058 --> 00:06:56.161
I followed her upstairs and down, admiring as I went, for all was well arranged and handsome.

112
00:06:57.262 --> 00:07:02.724
The rooms on the third floor, though, were dark and small and filled with furniture long out of

113
00:07:02.784 --> 00:07:10.348
style. All this—plus the lone window at the end of the corridor—gave that floor an air of gloom.

114
00:07:12.168 --> 00:07:17.470
Mrs. Fairfax led me up onto the flat roof of the house, which offered a fine view of

115
00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:18.991
the surrounding countryside.

116
00:07:20.131 --> 00:07:25.134
As I descended the steps to the third floor, she stayed behind to fasten the trapdoor.

117
00:07:26.414 --> 00:07:29.856
Suddenly I heard a strange, mirthless laugh.

118
00:07:31.156 --> 00:07:33.057
Startled, I called out to Mrs.

119
00:07:33.097 --> 00:07:34.938
Fairfax as she came downstairs.

120
00:07:34.958 --> 00:07:37.099
"Did you hear that laugh?"

121
00:07:37.119 --> 00:07:39.780
"Oh, that's one of the servants.

122
00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.882
Grace Poole sews up here, and she and Leah are often noisy together."

123
00:07:47.082 --> 00:07:51.243
Just then I heard the laugh again followed by an odd murmur.

124
00:07:51.263 --> 00:07:54.404
"Grace!" exclaimed Mrs.

125
00:07:54.464 --> 00:07:58.645
Fairfax. "Are you sure you don't have any ghosts in this house?"

126
00:07:59.086 --> 00:08:00.006
I asked nervously.

127
00:08:00.026 --> 00:08:02.607
"Quite sure," Mrs.

128
00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:03.747
Fairfax replied.

129
00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:06.848
"Come along to lunch, my dear."
